==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːpə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person or a thing who [[crawl]]s or creeps along the ground.
# Often in plural, a one-piece [[garment]] for infants designed to facilitate access to the wearer's diaper. 
# A device which allows a small child to safely roam around a room from a seated or standing position.
# A metal plate with [[spike|spikes]], designed to be worn with shoes to prevent [[slip|slipping]].
# {{botany}} Any [[plant]] (as [[ivy]] or [[periwinkle]]) that grows by [[creep]]ing; especially a climbing plant of the genus ''[[Parthenocissus]]''.
# A [[treecreeper]].
# {{nautical}} A small, four-hooked [[grapnel]] used to recover objects dropped onto the sea bed.
# The lowest gear of a tractor or truck, also [[creeper gear]], [[creeper shift]].
# A low-profile, wheeled [[platform]] whereupon an [[auto mechanic]] may lie on their back and gain better access to the underbody of a vehicle.

====Quotations====
* ''Then the piglet tore loose from the '''creepers''' and scurried into the undergrowth.'' - "[[w:Lord of the Flies|Lord of the Flies]]" (1964) by [[w:William Golding|William Golding]]

